how widely people scatter around it, not a prediction for a person.","The drug effect is the researcher's stated hypothesis, converted into the model's terms; it is not a prediction for any compound.","The parameters are the 2013 CAMD estimates released with adsim 3.0 (posterior draws, not re-estimated). With them the engine reproduces the EMA qualification opinion 2013 Tables 7, 9 and 11, not Table 10's intervals or Figures 15 and 16.","The FDA letter (2013-06-12) and the EMA qualification opinion (adopted 2013-09-19) concern the original tool in its context of use; no regulatory status transfers to this implementation.","Context of the model: mild and moderate Alzheimer disease, ADAS-cog 11 (0 to 70, higher is worse), trials of up to two years.","The assurance counts every significant benefit over the effects the stated distribution allows, a null or an irrelevant effect included: it is not the chance that the drug works, and it is not the chance that a development programme succeeds.","More simulated trials shrink only the Monte Carlo error of this number; they do not change a wrong distribution or a wrong model.","Draws the model cannot represent were redrawn (the distribution is truncated to what it can); the share is in the result.","This effect is what follows if the published chain for aducanumab holds (serum model, amyloid PET model, and the trial-level association between amyloid PET and ADAS-Cog). It is never a statement that the drug works.","The link's evidence is on a mixture of ADAS-Cog versions and the CDR-SB, while this model is ADAS-cog 11: the scale does not match.","The link comes from trials mostly in early Alzheimer disease (MMSE 20 to 30); this model describes mild-to-moderate disease (MMSE 14 to 26): the population does not match.","The link was fitted on the same trials the chain is checked against, so agreement with their results is not independent of it.","The link is an association across trials, not the causal effect of lowering amyloid in one person.","The serum and amyloid PET models reproduce the SUVR change the paper prints for its reference patient and the change reported for EMERGE's high dose at week 78 within a few hundredths; the paper's own statement of the time to a SUVR of 1.10 is not reproduced from its published parameters."]}}}
